WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.942 --> 00:00:04.580
- [Guide] On your left, on your left.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.020
- [Narrator] These
lifelike dinosaur puppets

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.550
will star in the new
"Jurassic World Live Tour,"

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.823
which debuts in arenas
around the US this fall.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.450
The show is produced
by Feld Entertainment,

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.320
the same company behind "Disney on Ice"

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.263
and "Marvel Universe Live."

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.407
- I would like to officially
introduce all of you to Jeanie.

00:00:26.407 --> 00:00:29.870
- [Ross] You're gonna be
face-to-face with actual dinosaurs.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.210
We've done a lot of
development, a lot of research

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.840
to making these dinosaurs really lifelike.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.050
The texture of their skin,
their eyes, the way they move,

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:42.409
the speed at which they move,
everything is super realistic.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.040
- [Narrator] The show's scenic team

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.550
designed the dinosaur puppets

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.240
using the CGI models of the creatures

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.493
seen in the "Jurassic" film franchise.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.330
- There's a foam underlayer
that houses all the electronics

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:56.870
and gives it the shape that's needed,

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.510
and then we cover the entirety of it

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:00.400
in its scaling pattern, its skin.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.300
It's really impressive to
see even the little nuances,

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.560
the eye blinks, the little
cock to the head to the side.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.910
The idea is that you can see
what the dinosaur is feeling

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.043
by what that "dinoteer"
is doing internally.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.990
- [Narrator] The puppets
are controlled by dinoteers

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.290
who not only have to act like dinosaurs,

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:20.770
they also have to be in
incredible physical condition

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.870
because the costumes
weigh over 100 pounds.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.170
- Make no mistake, these
are absolutely athletes,

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.530
and they are elite athletes at that.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:29.660
They have diverse backgrounds,

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.360
whether that be from exceptional training

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.270
in martial arts, dance, gymnastics.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:36.500
- They need to be super
fit to wear that weight

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:40.210
and to really move and feel
it very light on their feet,

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:43.820
even though they have 120
additional pounds on their body.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.290
- [Narrator] The team gave our producer

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.800
a 60-pound weighted vest to get a sense

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.660
of what the costume feels
like for the dinoteers.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.780
- Careful with those threads,
that's J. Crew Factory.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.613
- [Jay] We're gonna ask you to be

00:01:54.613 --> 00:01:56.180
in a very unnatural position.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.750
This is not a normal position
for a human being to be in

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:02.029
if they're manipulating
and being a dinoteer.

00:02:02.029 --> 00:02:03.300
- So now you're gonna step forward.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.930
- A lot of it's in sort
of a semi-squat position,

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.340
and their gait is much larger, much wider.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.540
So these cause excessive
stress on joints and backs

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.526
and things of that nature as well.

00:02:13.526 --> 00:02:14.359
- OK.

00:02:14.359 --> 00:02:15.298
I should have...

00:02:15.298 --> 00:02:16.748
should have done some lunges.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.210
- [Narrator] Along with familiar faces

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:23.070
like Blue the Velociraptor,
the show will introduce

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.610
a new character to the
"Jurassic" universe:

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.820
a Troodon named Jeanie.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:28.950
- [Dan] So we've got a Troodon.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.050
Troodons were believed to be

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.970
the most intelligent dinosaur that lived.

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:34.950
So our lead character is
a dinosaur called Jeanie,

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:37.530
short for genius, and she
really forms the backbone

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:40.230
of our story, and it's her
intelligence which really

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:43.573
inspired us in what to
explore with our new story.

00:02:44.815 --> 00:02:45.700
- Easy.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.930
- This is truly a marriage
of the fundamentals

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.810
of hand puppetry with the fundamentals

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.800
of full-body character work.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:53.610
So these bike brakes here are responsible

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.530
for the head looking side-to-side.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:58.080
It is a multistep process to train a human

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.180
to walk like a dinosaur. That is for sure.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.853
A lot of it starts with
out-of-costume work first.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.370
- [Narrator] Before the dinoteers suit up,

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.797
they practice fundamental
movements with hand puppets.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:14.470
- There you go!

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:15.840
We're looking for people not only

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.550
with those strengths and stamina

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.530
but also people who can really
manage sensory overload,

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:24.640
working inside confined
costumes in the dark

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.730
with limited hearing, limited vision,

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.200
while being taxed physically.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.000
- [Narrator] So these dinosaurs
look amazing close-up.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.970
But how will they look for people

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.485
sitting in the cheap seats?

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.680
- It's so important that everyone

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.570
who comes to the "Jurassic
World Live Tour,"

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:42.800
no matter where they're sitting,

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.120
that they have a great experience.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.440
We make sure that all the
dinosaurs, all the show elements

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.020
have a really high level of detail

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.100
that actually makes it read from far away

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.400
no matter where they are
positioned in the arena.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.270
- [Narrator] The show promises one element

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.390
that people watching from the rafters

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:58.303
will definitely be able to see.

00:04:00.964 --> 00:04:04.780
A full-size animatronic
T-rex, which, at the time

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.443
of this report, was still
being built and tested.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.170
- [Interviewer] Can you give
me an idea of what it costs

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.860
to create a lifelike
animatronic Tyrannosaurus rex?

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.032
- No.
- North of a million?

00:04:16.032 --> 00:04:16.865
- Yes.

00:04:16.865 --> 00:04:18.330
- North of 10 million?

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:19.530
- Not gonna answer anymore.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.550
- Got it, OK.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.380
- [Narrator] The producer
wouldn't give specifics

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.130
about the budget, but she did say

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.240
it's one of the most expensive shows

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.220
the company has ever produced

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:31.400
and even referenced a famous
quote from "Jurassic Park."

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.550
- We have spared no
expense on this production.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:34.640
- Spared no expense.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:35.710
Spared no expense.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.890
Spared no expense.

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:39.598
- Dinosaurs are pretty expensive.

00:04:39.598 --> 00:04:41.181
- Careful, careful.

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:44.801
- Selfie?

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:47.179
- Oh, OK, now he's taking a selfie.

00:04:47.179 --> 00:04:50.123
I don't know how she'll
react to that, but we'll see.

